                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of Mexican horseman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d76d14b-da05-4432-9822-d6b2b2b0e968",
                                "sense_id": "74710a90-47b9-36f1-bdd0-40fd8b879c37",
                                "text": "The star is Jorge Negrete, a tall baritone with a pencil mustache who appeared as a singing charro in a few dozen ranchero musicals."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b4a8ec9-cab8-4adf-8576-d6251da857cd",
                                "sense_id": "74710a90-47b9-36f1-bdd0-40fd8b879c37",
                                "text": "The show features a revolving roster of \"freaks\" both born and made: at Ozzfest the former included Jessie the Half-Boy; a \"wolf-boy\" from Mexico dressed in a charro suit and sombrero; and the aforementioned Punkin Head, aka Scott the Cyclops, who capitalizes on his empty eye socket with various props including, as Harck promises, his own tongue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8be1b56b-898d-40c9-aee1-fac17b342449",
                                "sense_id": "74710a90-47b9-36f1-bdd0-40fd8b879c37",
                                "text": "But he's also evolved from the mythic Mexican cowboy of the 19th century, the charro, who even if he had nothing else had balls."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
